        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "df5806d2-84c8-5445-b45b-34dca96887f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Chinese Chongqing Dog, Kanni, Tugou, Chinese Field Dog, Xiasi Dog\n- Places: China, Tamil Nadu, Zami River, Kyondaw, Phadaw, Apalon, Kanni, Danon, Kyain Seikgyi, Chaunghanakwa, Mon State\n- Concepts: dog breed uses, indigenous sighthounds, native dog breeds, river flow\n\nFacts:\n- The Chinese Chongqing Dog was used in its early years for hunting wild boar and rabbits.\n- The Chinese Chongqing Dog is now used in China to protect families and belongings.\n- The Kanni is a rare indigenous South Indian sighthound breed of dog found in the state of Tamil Nadu.\n- The name Kanni means maiden.\n- The Kanni breed is used mainly for coursing game.\n- Tugou includes the Chinese Field Dog, the Chinese Chongqing Dog, the Xiasi Dog, and several other native dog breeds distributed across China.\n- The Chinese Field Dog is described as the most popular Chinese dog breed within Tugou.\n- The Zami River flows north past Kyondaw, Phadaw, Apalon, Kanni, Danon, Kyain Seikgyi, and Chaunghanakwa before flowing into Mon State.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "df392f31-7212-52ea-9bee-4948389e0512",
